{#
 Shared brand block (logo + hostname wordmark).

 BYTE by ACE override of luci-theme-footstrap's
 ucode/template/themes/footstrap/partials/brand.ut (Apache-2.0; that file lives in
 the theme package and is installed to /usr/share/ucode/luci/template/themes/
 footstrap/partials/brand.ut, where this copy wins). MODIFIED: the inline OpenWrt
 arcs are replaced with the BYTE "B" mark so the header matches the tab favicon,
 the PWA icon and logo.svg instead of advertising OpenWrt. The include contract
 (`boardinfo`, `dispatcher`) is unchanged, so header.ut and sysauth.ut keep
 working untouched.

 Note for upgrades: an `opkg upgrade luci-theme-footstrap` reinstalls the theme's
 own copy over this one until the next sysupgrade. The build gate asserts the
 theme still ships a brand partial, so a rename upstream fails the build instead
 of silently reverting to the OpenWrt mark.
-#}
<a class="fs-brand" href="{{ dispatcher.build_url() }}">
	<span class="fs-logo">
		{# The BYTE "B": stem plus two bowls, counters punched with the even-odd
		   rule, underlined in the theme accent. Same geometry as logo.svg
		   (256x256), cropped to the glyph. No font, no extra request, and the
		   glyph follows the theme text colour through currentColor, so it reads
		   on light and dark without a second asset. #}
		<svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="60 40 120 176"><path fill="currentColor" fill-rule="evenodd" d="M72 52h12a10 10 0 0 1 10 10v108a10 10 0 0 1-10 10H72zM98 52h18a26 26 0 0 1 26 26v12a26 26 0 0 1-26 26H98zM112 66h4a9 9 0 0 1 9 9v6a9 9 0 0 1-9 9h-4zM98 108h18a30 30 0 0 1 30 30v12a30 30 0 0 1-30 30H98zM112 122h4a11 11 0 0 1 11 11v4a11 11 0 0 1-11 11h-4z"/><rect x="72" y="192" width="100" height="12" rx="6" fill="#00b5e2"/></svg>
	</span>
	<span class="fs-wordmark">{{ entityencode(striptags(boardinfo.hostname ?? 'BYTE'), true) }}</span>
</a>
